- defines(v1, "availability ok?", {"No", "Yes"}) & guard(b1, n6, v1 = 'No'), guard(b1, n7, v1 = 'Yes'): Uses "No"/"Yes" instead of the source's explicit values "nok"/"ok". Contradicts: 'If the availability is "nok"... if the availability is "ok"'
- action(n1, "start booking service"): Hallucinates an initial step. Source states 'start by booking a bus', indicating that booking the bus is the first documented process step.
- action(n6, "end booking due to unavailable bus") & action(n8, "end booking complete"): Hallucinates terminal behavioral steps. Source simply states the process concludes ('the process of booking the bus will end' / 'process will come to an end'), which should map directly to end nodes without intermediate actions.